# CSS Modules and styling

Use CSS Modules for component styles. Do not add Tailwind, Sass, or CSS-in-JS. `postcss-preset-mantine` is allowed (`rem()`, `@mixin`, `light-dark()`).

```
tokens → reset → shared primitives → colocated component modules
```

- One `.module.css` per component; one class, one job (`root`, `title`, `actions`)
- Colocate `Component.tsx` with `Component.module.css`
- Tokens, reset, and primitives live under `styles/`
- Compose shared primitives **into** components. Never import another component's `.module.css`
- Modules use `--mantine-*` or semantic aliases in `styles/tokens.css`. No raw hex/rgb/oklch
- camelCase classes; `composes` first in a rule; no circular `composes`; nesting at most two levels; no IDs or `!important`
- `:global` only for third-party hooks. Never wrap a whole module in `:global`

Declare `@layer reset, tokens, primitives;` in the global entry. Wrap shared styles in those layers. Leave colocated component modules **unlayered**.

## Agent do / don't

**Do**

- Colocate a module with its component
- Compose primitives; override in the unlayered local module
- Verify visual changes in the browser

**Don't**

- Add Tailwind, Sass, or CSS-in-JS
- Import another component's `.module.css`
- Use unscoped global class names (`.button`, `.wrapper`)

```css
.root {
  composes: stack from '../../../../styles/primitives.module.css';
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--color-text);
}
```

```css
/* Bad — sibling-module coupling; kebab-case; :global leak */
.cta-button {
  composes: padded from '../Card/Card.module.css';
}

:global(.button) {
  color: #228b22;
}
```
